<code>assert !\old(this.contains(o)) => !\result;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(this.contains(o)) => !\result;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(this.contains(o)) => !this.remove(o);</code>

However, the comment seems to have a mistake. It states that "If the element was present before removal, the method returns false," which contradicts the actual behavior of the `remove` method. The method should return `true` if the element was present and removed. Therefore, the correct assert statement should be:

<code>assert \old(this.contains(o)) => this.remove(o);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(this.contains(o)) => !this.remove(o);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !\old(this.contains(o)) => !this.remove(o);</code>
